00:35:31.656 --> 00:35:33.964
-IAN: Yeah.
-BEAR: Did you talk to her?

759
00:35:33.999 --> 00:35:35.897
-IAN: Yeah. I did.
-BEAR: What did she say?

760
00:35:35.932 --> 00:35:38.458
Uh. sh-she's... she's good.

761
00:35:38.493 --> 00:35:39.959
Everything's good.

762
00:35:39.995 --> 00:35:42.233
She wasn't. like.
looking at you or anything.

763
00:35:42.268 --> 00:35:44.733
She was staring at me. and...

764
00:35:44.768 --> 00:35:47.073
Maybe. but I-I was just
talking to her.

765
00:35:47.108 --> 00:35:48.902
She was looking at both of us.

766
00:35:48.937 --> 00:35:51.372
It looked like we were
talking about her.

767
00:35:51.408 --> 00:35:52.815
so that explains it.

768
00:35:52.850 --> 00:35:54.215
You guys walked in together.

769
00:35:54.250 --> 00:35:55.578
-I'm gonna just call her.
-Uh. maybe don't.

770
00:35:55.613 --> 00:35:57.120
-(knocking at door)
-Don't do that.

771
00:35:57.155 --> 00:35:57.950
'Cause. you know.
we're just... we're chatting.

772
00:35:57.985 --> 00:35:59.418
-Just...
-Hold on.

773
00:35:59.453 --> 00:36:00.415
It sounds like you're
gonna talk to her.

774
00:36:00.450 --> 00:36:01.884
-Bear...
-(phone beeps)

775
00:36:06.963 --> 00:36:09.261
-NIKKI: Hey. Bear.
-Oh.

776
00:36:09.297 --> 00:36:10.756
-(chuckles): Hey.
-I had to shower.

777
00:36:10.792 --> 00:36:12.532
and I didn't know what to wear.

778
00:36:13.537 --> 00:36:15.205
For what?

779
00:36:16.207 --> 00:36:18.403
So. I'm really sorry
about last night. I. um...

780
00:36:18.439 --> 00:36:20.373
-No. -Ian told me
you were freaked out.

781
00:36:20.408 --> 00:36:24.005
I'm just glad I could
be there. I guess.

782
00:36:24.041 --> 00:36:28.350
Yeah. um. so I probably
shouldn't have taken anything.

783
00:36:32.116 --> 00:36:33.919
So...

784
00:36:33.955 --> 00:36:36.523
I was on MDMA.

785
00:36:37.620 --> 00:36:40.588
-Right.
-And... wasted.

786
00:36:40.623 --> 00:36:42.265
(chuckles):
That's okay.

787
00:36:43.633 --> 00:36:45.568
Do you...

788
00:36:45.603 --> 00:36:48.471
remember...

789
00:36:48.506 --> 00:36:49.965
stuff?

790
00:36:50.940 --> 00:36:53.376
Some of it. I mean...

791
00:36:53.411 --> 00:36:56.676
So. if I was weird. that's why.
and my dad made me a mess.

792
00:36:56.712 --> 00:36:58.709
and so I did things I probably
wouldn't have done otherwise.

793
00:36:58.745 --> 00:37:00.610
And I'm not saying
that you took advantage of me.

794
00:37:00.646 --> 00:37:03.416
Nikki. I didn't know
you were on drugs.

795
00:37:03.452 --> 00:37:04.879
That's what I'm saying.
I'm not saying that.

796
00:37:04.914 --> 00:37:07.119
-Not saying what?
-You took advantage of me.

797
00:37:07.155 --> 00:37:09.022
I don't think... I didn't.

798
00:37:09.057 --> 00:37:10.289
I know. That's why...

799
00:37:10.324 --> 00:37:12.187
-I'm saying you didn't.
-Okay.

800
00:37:12.222 --> 00:37:13.830
Good.

801
00:37:13.865 --> 00:37:18.026
I just. um. don't like to...

802
00:37:19.332 --> 00:37:20.796
I really like what we have.

803
00:37:20.831 --> 00:37:22.532
and I want to be honest
about some things.

804
00:37:22.568 --> 00:37:24.700
and it's really important
for me.

805
00:37:24.735 --> 00:37:27.574
It's okay.
Um. you know. I-I get it.

806
00:37:28.843 --> 00:37:30.346
I get it.

807
00:37:31.948 --> 00:37:34.077
I know you like me. Bear.

808
00:37:34.113 --> 00:37:36.176
♪ ♪

809
00:37:38.689 --> 00:37:40.356
(stammers)

810
00:37:41.691 --> 00:37:43.260
No. I...

811
00:37:44.554 --> 00:37:46.263
Why? Do you like me?

812
00:37:49.892 --> 00:37:52.269
Would it freak you out
if I said yes?

813
00:37:54.266 --> 00:37:56.229
(chuckles softly)

814
00:37:59.944 --> 00:38:02.373
How long have you felt that way?

815
00:38:02.408 --> 00:38:04.210
It's just happened over time.

816
00:38:04.245 --> 00:38:06.882
Started during Christmas. and...

817
00:38:06.917 --> 00:38:08.546
I don't know. it just...

818
00:38:08.582 --> 00:38:10.947
Then. last night.
I saw what we could...

819
00:38:17.159 --> 00:38:18.889
Do you have feelings for me?

820
00:38:28.002 --> 00:38:29.803
Yeah. I do.

821
00:38:29.839 --> 00:38:31.935
♪ ♪

822
00:38:33.239 --> 00:38:35.312
(voices muted)

823
00:38:42.280 --> 00:38:44.651
♪ ♪

824
00:38:49.694 --> 00:38:53.330
♪ ♪

825
00:39:03.103 --> 00:39:05.133
♪ ♪

826
00:39:21.053 --> 00:39:23.684
And I wrote. "In a band."
and then she made me change it.

827
00:39:23.719 --> 00:39:25.327
-Yeah.
-Bitch. (laughs)

828
00:39:25.363 --> 00:39:27.294
And then you leaned in.
and you whispered...

829
00:39:27.329 --> 00:39:29.292
BOTH:
"I'll be in your band."

830
00:39:29.327 --> 00:39:30.864
(both laugh)

831
00:39:30.899 --> 00:39:32.798
Yeah.

832
00:39:34.532 --> 00:39:35.999
How's your dad doing?

833
00:39:37.970 --> 00:39:40.137
-Can we not talk about that?
-(cell phone vibrating)

834
00:39:40.172 --> 00:39:41.378
Okay.

835
00:39:43.373 --> 00:39:45.211
Um...

836
00:39:45.247 --> 00:39:48.545
so what do you want to do?

837
00:39:48.580 --> 00:39:50.712
I mean. I never really asked.

838
00:39:50.747 --> 00:39:52.947
Well. that's not all your fault.

839
00:39:52.982 --> 00:39:55.856
I mean. I'm kind of private.
I guess.

840
00:39:55.892 --> 00:39:57.486
You guess?

841
00:39:57.521 --> 00:39:59.719
I've been told.

842
00:39:59.754 --> 00:40:01.291
-By who?
-Ian.

843
00:40:01.327 --> 00:40:03.493
You. actually.

844
00:40:03.528 --> 00:40:04.733
You told me that once.

845
00:40:04.768 --> 00:40:06.436
I did?

846
00:40:08.402 --> 00:40:11.001
You called me a closed book.

847
00:40:11.036 --> 00:40:13.240
Well. I guess the good thing
about a closed book is

848
00:40:13.275 --> 00:40:15.104
I get to read it from the start.

849
00:40:16.407 --> 00:40:17.579
(chuckles)

850
00:40:20.218 --> 00:40:22.183
Maybe a food critic
or something.

851
00:40:22.218 --> 00:40:23.516
You put ketchup on your steak.

852
00:40:23.551 --> 00:40:24.647
I'll come in.
and they'll be like.

853
00:40:24.683 --> 00:40:26.313
"Hey. aren't you the food guy?"

854
00:40:26.348 --> 00:40:27.918
And I'll say. "Please.
call me Three-Bite Bailey."

855
00:40:27.954 --> 00:40:29.523
And then they will serve me
a four-course meal.

856
00:40:29.558 --> 00:40:31.350
and I'll pull out my wallet.
and they'll say.

857
00:40:31.386 --> 00:40:33.819
"No. no. no. sir. please.
tonight. on the house."

858
00:40:33.855 --> 00:40:35.063
And then I get paid.

859
00:40:35.098 --> 00:40:36.760
Is that how that goes?

860
00:40:36.796 --> 00:40:38.760
-I actually don't know.
-(both laughing)

861
00:40:38.795 --> 00:40:40.763
Okay. my little food critic.

862
00:40:40.799 --> 00:40:42.103
what's the verdict
on this bread?

863
00:40:42.138 --> 00:40:43.738
-This bread?
-Mm-hmm.

864
00:40:43.774 --> 00:40:44.938
Oh.

865
00:40:44.973 --> 00:40:46.806
Well...

866
00:40:49.438 --> 00:40:52.876
Hmm. Slightly stale. but the
butter makes up for that shit.

867
00:40:52.911 --> 00:40:54.740
-Profound.
-That'll be a hundred dollars.

868
00:40:54.776 --> 00:40:56.042
(laughs) Well...

869
00:40:56.078 --> 00:40:57.817
-(cell phone vibrating)
-Sorry.

870
00:40:59.455 --> 00:41:00.956
It's the second time
he's called.

871
00:41:00.992 --> 00:41:02.151
I'll be right back.

872
00:41:03.419 --> 00:41:06.126
-What is it. dude? I'm busy.
-IAN: Oh. busy doing Nikki?

873
00:41:06.161 --> 00:41:07.556
What do you want?

874
00:41:07.591 --> 00:41:10.297
Okay. so. um...

875
00:41:10.333 --> 00:41:11.960
-What is it?
-(Ian stammers)

876
00:41:11.995 --> 00:41:13.566
I'm not gonna tell Sarah
about this.

877
00:41:13.601 --> 00:41:16.437
because I don't want
to spread drama.

878
00:41:16.473 --> 00:41:19.306
I looked into Nikki's dad
having cancer.

879
00:41:19.341 --> 00:41:21.705
and he's healthy as a baby.

880
00:41:21.741 --> 00:41:23.942
He's been to work.
like. every day.

881
00:41:30.287 --> 00:41:31.978
Why would she lie
about that. Ian?

882
00:41:32.013 --> 00:41:33.587
I don't know. For attention.

883
00:41:33.622 --> 00:41:35.216
I called the hospital
she told me about.

884
00:41:35.251 --> 00:41:38.055
and they didn't even know
who I was talking about.

885
00:41:38.090 --> 00:41:40.927
Look. you know I always
got your back on this stuff.

886
00:41:40.962 --> 00:41:44.826
Apparently. Nikki and Sarah
had a conversation about you

887
00:41:44.861 --> 00:41:46.402
that-that day you weren't in.

888
00:41:46.438 --> 00:41:49.129
and. uh. Nikki said
she just thought of you

889
00:41:49.165 --> 00:41:51.437
like her little brother
or. you know.

890
00:41:51.472 --> 00:41:52.803
and she. like. friend-zoned you.

891
00:41:52.839 --> 00:41:54.838
And-and-and look.
that may suck to hear.

892
00:41:54.873 --> 00:41:56.745
but I just think
you got to know because.

893
00:41:56.781 --> 00:41:59.107
I-I don't know. I think she has
some kind of ill intentions

894
00:41:59.143 --> 00:42:01.681
or something freaking mental
is going on. man.

895
00:42:01.716 --> 00:42:03.344
And maybe Sarah's jealous
and made that up.

896
00:42:03.379 --> 00:42:06.022
but. like. even if you take
that out of the equation.

897
00:42:06.057 --> 00:42:09.184
this is strange. dude.

898
00:42:09.219 --> 00:42:11.493
It's like Nikki snapped
into a different person.

899
00:42:11.528 --> 00:42:14.159
Sh-She's all of a sudden
infatuated with you.

900
00:42:14.195 --> 00:42:16.225
♪ ♪

901
00:42:30.179 --> 00:42:31.944
Everything okay?

902
00:42:38.081 --> 00:42:40.381
(voice trembling):
Nikki. do you...

903
00:42:42.354 --> 00:42:44.319
What?

904
00:42:45.523 --> 00:42:47.492
Never mind.

905
00:42:47.527 --> 00:42:50.033
I have something for you.

906
00:42:50.068 --> 00:42:52.063
-What is it?
-Um...

907
00:43:00.571 --> 00:43:01.941
What is it?

908
00:43:03.914 --> 00:43:05.780
Open it.

909
00:43:11.519 --> 00:43:14.321
It's a... it's a tiger's eye.

910
00:43:14.357 --> 00:43:16.521
-Wow.
-It was my mom's.

911
00:43:16.556 --> 00:43:18.992
and then it was mine.

912
00:43:19.027 --> 00:43:24.233
It's supposed to bring you
confidence and willpower. so...

913
00:43:24.268 --> 00:43:26.394
now you can be a food critic.

914
00:43:29.240 --> 00:43:30.934
Why are you giving it to me?

915
00:43:30.969 --> 00:43:35.004
Bear. I love you
so. so. so. so. so much.

916
00:43:35.040 --> 00:43:37.273
I don't think I could live
without you.

917
00:43:41.882 --> 00:43:44.621
You love me more
than anyone in the world?

918
00:43:48.888 --> 00:43:51.221
(chuckling):
Yes. more than anyone.

919
00:43:54.657 --> 00:43:55.995
Nikki.

920
00:43:57.198 --> 00:43:59.028
Yeah?

921
00:43:59.063 --> 00:44:01.035
Does your dad
really have cancer?

922
00:44:01.071 --> 00:44:03.101
♪ ♪

923
00:44:15.480 --> 00:44:16.752
No.

924
00:44:20.489 --> 00:44:22.892
(chuckling):
No. no. no.

925
00:44:22.927 --> 00:44:24.059
What?

926
00:44:24.094 --> 00:44:25.987
No. no. no.

927
00:44:26.022 --> 00:44:28.431
-no. no. no. no. no.
-What?

928
00:44:28.466 --> 00:44:30.294
-Don't do that!
-Nikki. (stammers)

929
00:44:30.330 --> 00:44:32.735
-I thought we were having a
nice date. -(patrons murmuring)

930
00:44:32.770 --> 00:44:34.495
-We-we are. We are. Sit down.
-Why does it matter?

931
00:44:34.531 --> 00:44:37.835
-I thought we were having
a nice date. -We are. We are.

932
00:44:37.870 --> 00:44:39.634
-We are. We are.
-(Nikki crying)

933
00:44:39.670 --> 00:44:41.803
It's okay.

934
00:44:41.838 --> 00:44:44.208
We are. We are.

935
00:44:54.291 --> 00:44:56.055
Then why does it matter?

936
00:45:04.268 --> 00:45:05.662
It doesn't matter to me.

937
00:45:05.697 --> 00:45:08.368
(grunts) Oh. yeah.

938
00:45:08.404 --> 00:45:10.564
(grunting. moaning)

939
00:45:12.267 --> 00:45:14.876
-(Bear grunting)
-Yeah. Uh-huh.

940
00:45:15.980 --> 00:45:18.011
(moaning)

941
00:45:19.580 --> 00:45:21.682
(breathing heavily)

942
00:45:21.717 --> 00:45:24.017
-Oh. that was amazing. baby.
-Yeah.

943
00:45:27.057 --> 00:45:28.516
Yeah.

944
00:45:38.093 --> 00:45:40.231
(takes deep breath)

945
00:46:00.750 --> 00:46:02.121
Nikki?

946
00:46:16.806 --> 00:46:18.907
-NIKKI: Go back to sleep.
-(Bear gasps)

947
00:46:20.409 --> 00:46:21.811
BEAR:
Nikki.

948
00:46:26.548 --> 00:46:28.312
What are you doing?

949
00:46:34.259 --> 00:46:36.218
What are you doing?

950
00:46:36.253 --> 00:46:37.959
(whispering):
Watching you sleep.

951
00:46:39.056 --> 00:46:40.929
You're so cute when you sleep.

952
00:46:43.400 --> 00:46:44.859
Wearing my sweater. huh?

953
00:46:44.895 --> 00:46:46.462
Smells like you.

954
00:46:50.641 --> 00:46:52.941
-Can you come back to bed?
-No. no.

955
00:46:58.777 --> 00:47:00.278
-Nikki.
-No.

956
00:47:04.589 --> 00:47:07.285
(crying):
I don't like my dreams.

957
00:47:08.620 --> 00:47:11.289
(sobbing)

958
00:47:17.098 --> 00:47:21.535
I feel like you don't love me
as much as I do.

959
00:47:21.570 --> 00:47:26.106
Like it's not mutual.

960
00:47:27.102 --> 00:47:29.668
No. I... I do.

961
00:47:29.704 --> 00:47:32.411
-Just come back to bed.
-(sobbing continues)

962
00:47:32.446 --> 00:47:34.048
Please?

963
00:47:35.286 --> 00:47:37.051
(sobbing stops)

964
00:47:42.185 --> 00:47:44.788
(crying):
Go back to sleep.

965
00:47:44.824 --> 00:47:46.159
(Nikki sobs softly)

966
00:48:09.752 --> 00:48:13.522
-Why don't you love me?!
-(gasps)

967
00:48:13.557 --> 00:48:16.189
Nikki? Nikki. where are you?

968
00:48:18.727 --> 00:48:21.194
(rapid. trembling breaths)

969
00:48:24.894 --> 00:48:26.232
What?

970
00:48:31.399 --> 00:48:33.371
Nikki. what are you doing?

971
00:48:37.709 --> 00:48:39.179
Nikki.

972
00:48:41.576 --> 00:48:43.513
No. what-what do you
want me to do?

973
00:48:44.883 --> 00:48:46.516
For Sandy. okay?

974
00:48:53.055 --> 00:48:55.096
♪ ♪

975
00:49:14.108 --> 00:49:16.612
Stay!

976
00:49:20.952 --> 00:49:22.992
(insects trilling)

977
00:49:25.121 --> 00:49:27.161
(birds chirping)

978
00:49:36.473 --> 00:49:38.106
What the fuck?

979
00:49:51.248 --> 00:49:53.154
-Morning.
-NIKKI: Morning.

980
00:49:55.690 --> 00:49:56.993
(clears throat)

981
00:49:59.087 --> 00:50:00.724
Um...

982
00:50:00.759 --> 00:50:02.031
Yeah?

983
00:50:05.360 --> 00:50:07.929
Did you cut my hair?

984
00:50:07.964 --> 00:50:09.236
Yeah.

985
00:50:13.675 --> 00:50:16.177
Let's not do that.

986
00:50:21.879 --> 00:50:23.349
Okay.

987
00:50:28.625 --> 00:50:30.489
Packed you a lunch.

988
00:50:30.525 --> 00:50:31.690
Oh.

989
00:50:31.726 --> 00:50:33.126
(Nikki laughs)

990
00:50:33.161 --> 00:50:36.465
Oh. oh. can-can we talk
about last night?

991
00:50:36.500 --> 00:50:38.797
(sighs) I know.

992
00:50:38.832 --> 00:50:40.096
I know. I know.

993
00:50:40.131 --> 00:50:41.404
It was kind of weird.

994
00:50:41.439 --> 00:50:42.702
Right? (chuckles)

995
00:50:42.738 --> 00:50:44.832
Yeah. I'm so sorry.

996
00:50:46.306 --> 00:50:48.467
Okay. good.
'cause if I'm being honest.

997
00:50:48.503 --> 00:50:50.005
it was kind of terrifying.

998
00:50:50.040 --> 00:50:51.212
Oh. my God.

999
00:50:52.175 --> 00:50:54.716
I'm so sorry.

1000
00:50:54.751 --> 00:50:57.812
I had a bad dream. and I just...

1001
00:51:03.386 --> 00:51:05.556
-You what?
-How's this?

1002
00:51:16.033 --> 00:51:17.370
Not great.

1003
00:51:18.639 --> 00:51:19.840
Okay.

1004
00:51:19.876 --> 00:51:21.204
-Listen. Nikki.
-Come here.

1005
00:51:21.239 --> 00:51:23.411
-I think...
-Come here.

1006
00:51:23.446 --> 00:51:24.773
Listen.

1007
00:51:36.253 --> 00:51:38.427
(Bear's breath trembling)

1008
00:51:38.462 --> 00:51:40.319
I love you.

1009
00:51:40.355 --> 00:51:42.054
I love you. too.

1010
00:51:43.033 --> 00:51:45.126
-So. so. so. so...
-Okay. okay. okay. okay.

1011
00:51:45.161 --> 00:51:47.936
Good. Good.

1012
00:51:47.971 --> 00:51:50.096
So. will you promise me
something?

1013
00:51:50.132 --> 00:51:51.573
Yes.

1014
00:51:51.609 --> 00:51:53.870
No more weird stuff.

1015
00:51:53.906 --> 00:51:55.504
All right?

1016
00:51:55.539 --> 00:51:57.206
No more watching me
while I sleep

